DEFINITIONS AND KEY TERMS

To help explain things as clearly as possible in this End-User License Agreement, every time any of these terms are referenced, they are strictly defined as:

Cookie: a small amount of data generated by a website and saved by your web browser. It is used to identify your browser, provide analytics, and remember information about you such as your language preference or login information.
Company: when this Agreement mentions "Company," "we," "us," or "our," it refers to Aria Developer, that is responsible for the Application under this Agreement.
Country: where Aria Developer or the owners/founders of Aria are based — in this case, India.
Device: any internet-connected device such as a phone, tablet, computer, or any other device that can be used to access and use Aria.
Service: refers to the Aria mobile application provided by Aria Developer.
Third-party service: refers to advertisers, contest sponsors, promotional and marketing partners, and others who provide our content or whose products or services we think may interest you.
Application (the "App"): refers to Aria, the software mobile application provided by Aria Developer.
You: a person or entity that accesses or uses the Application.
